  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe browser tree's rows were pale grey on the light panel (#506).\n\n- **Root cause:** egui keeps a dark and a light style and follows the OS appearance. `theme::apply_to` wrote the token table only into the slot that was active at startup. On a Mac in light mode, egui switched to its stock light visuals while the painted tree kept drawing our table's ink on that panel. `apply_to` now writes the table into **both** slots, so the document's theme is the only theme.\n- **Row ink:** tree rows no longer use `text_faint`, the disabled tier, which reads about 3:1 on the light strip. A hidden row and the suffix use `text_dim`. A selected row is all `text`, because `text_dim` reads only 3.5:1 on the dark theme's selection fill. The rule lives in `painted::row_inks`.\n\n## How it was tested\n\n- New `egui_app::tree_ink_tests` (lib):\n  - `tree_row_ink_clears_body_contrast_on_every_row_ground`: every row ink clears WCAG body contrast (4.5:1) on every ground it is painted on (panel, strip, hover, selection), in both built-in themes.\n  - `applied_theme_fills_both_egui_theme_slots`: both egui slots carry the applied table, and flipping the OS theme keeps the table's panel fill.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick`, which escalated to batch, ran 9 steps. Green: geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion, app, ui integration suites, clippy `-D warnings` on all 8 crates.\n- Red in the `camcraft-ui` lib and binaries, all unrelated to this change:\n  - three headless tests that need a GPU adapter the gate machine did not provide: `headless_run_succeeds`, `egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`, `headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`;\n  - `structural::shell_structure_dark/light` (`\"v0.0.0\"` version label). These are confirmed red on current main too.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe look on a real screen, which needs a hands-on check in light and dark mode. That is why this PR stays a draft.\n\nChangelog: The browser tree's rows read clearly on the light theme; the theme no longer follows the OS appearance behind the user's back (#506)\n\nFixes #506\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
